  "answer_markdown": "Yes, there is a documented maximum number of concurrent token-stream tasks (referred to as **concurrent activity executions**) that a single workflow can run. This limit is controlled by the parameter `max_concurrent_scheduled_tasks`, which defaults to **100** for both the **List Executor Pattern** [1] and the **Offset Pagination Executor Pattern** [2].\n\nIf this limit is exceeded, the system will **not execute additional tasks concurrently** beyond the configured threshold. Instead, tasks will be queued and executed once the number of concurrent executions drops below the limit [3].\n\nFor example, if `max_concurrent_scheduled_tasks=100` and 101 tasks are scheduled simultaneously, only 100 will run concurrently, while the 101st task waits until one of the running tasks completes [3].\n\nThis behavior applies to both workflow executors mentioned in the documentation [1][2][3].",
