{
  "answer_markdown": "For the `POST /v1/chat/classifications` endpoint, the required fields in the `ChatClassificationRequest` body are as follows [1]:

- **`model`** (string, required) — The model to use for classification.
- **`input`** (ChatClassificationRequestInputs, required) — The chat to classify, structured as one of the following:
  - **`messages`** (array of objects, required) — When using the `InstructRequest` format, this must be an array of message objects, each containing:
    - `role` (string, required) — The role of the message (e.g., `user`, `assistant`).
    - `content` (string, required) — The content of the message.

  Example structure for `input`:
  ```json
  {
    "messages": [
      {"role": "user", "content": "I love this product!"}
    ]
  }
  ```

  The `labels` field is **not part of the request body** for this endpoint; it is used only in the dataset format for fine-tuning (as shown in source [2]) and not in the runtime classification request [1].

  **Note**: The `input` can also be an array of `InstructRequest` objects (e.g., for batch processing), but the core requirement for a single request is the `messages` array under `input` [1].",
