  "answer_markdown": "To fetch live data from a connected tool like **Gmail, Drive, or Notion** in Mistral's **Work chat**, you should use **[Connectors]** [1][2][4][5]. This feature acts as a **secure bridge** to retrieve, analyze, and act on real-time data from external tools without manually switching apps [2]. For example, you can ask Work to *\"Check my Gmail for unread messages about the quarterly report and summarize them\"* or *\"Find the latest design document in Google Drive and create a brief\"* [2][3][4][5].\n\n### Key Differences from **Web Search**\n- **Connectors** pull **live, structured data** from connected tools (e.g., Gmail, Notion) with **real-time updates** and **authentication approvals** before actions like sending emails or modifying data [2][4][5][6].\n- **Web Search** fetches **public, up-to-date answers** from the internet but does not interact with your private tools or data [1].\n\n### How to Use Connectors\n1. Enable the Connector in the chat by clicking the `+` icon or typing `/`, then selecting **Tools** and choosing the Connector (e.g., Gmail, Drive) [3].\n2. Describe your task naturally (e.g., *\"What meetings do I have tomorrow?\"* or *\"Find the latest Q3 revenue deck in Google Drive\"*) [3].\n3. Work will **automatically call the right Connector**, show **real-time progress**, and ask for **approvals** before sensitive actions [4][6][7].\n\n### Example Prompts for Connectors\n```\n- \"What meetings do I have tomorrow?\"\n- \"Find the latest Q3 revenue deck in Google Drive and prepare a one-page summary.\"\n- \"Check my unread emails from the legal team and draft replies for me to review.\"\n```\n\n### Transparency and Safety\n- Every Connector call is **visible in the chat**, showing inputs, outputs, and status (pending/succeeded/failed) [7].\n- Work may ask **clarifying questions** (e.g., *\"Which Connector should I use to find the contract: Notion or Google Drive?\"*) before proceeding [6].",
