For the `POST /v1/chat/classifications` endpoint, the **required fields** in the `ChatClassificationRequest` body are as follows [1]:

- **`model`** (string, required) — The model to use for classification.
- **`input`** (ChatClassificationRequestInputs, required) — The chat to classify, which can be one of the following:
  - **`messages`** (array of objects, required) — When using the `InstructRequest` format, this must be an array of message objects. Each message object must include:
    - `role` (string, required) — The role of the message (e.g., `user`, `assistant`).
    - `content` (string, required) — The content of the message.

  Example structure:
  ```json
  {
    "model": "your-model-name",
    "input": {
      "messages": [
        {"role": "user", "content": "I love this product!"}
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  The `input` can also be an **array of `InstructRequest` objects** (e.g., for multi-turn interactions).

  **Note:** The `labels` field is **not part of the request body** for this endpoint; it is used only in the dataset format for fine-tuning [2].

