  "answer_markdown": "To fetch live data from a connected tool like **Gmail, Drive, or Notion** in Mistral's **Work chat**, you should use **[Connectors]** [2]. This feature acts as a secure bridge to retrieve, analyze, and act on real-time data from external tools without manually switching between apps [2].\n\n### Key Differences from **Web Search**\n- **Connectors** pull **live, private data** from tools you’ve connected (e.g., Gmail, Notion, Google Drive) with your permissions [1][2].\n- **Web Search** fetches **public, up-to-date answers** from the internet but cannot access private or tool-specific data [1].\n\n### How to Use Connectors\n1. Enable a Connector in the chat by clicking the `+` icon or typing `/`, then selecting **Tools** and choosing the relevant Connector (e.g., Gmail, Notion) [3].\n2. Describe your task naturally (e.g., *“Check my unread Gmail messages about the quarterly report”*), and Work will automatically use the connected tool [3].\n\n**Example Prompts for Connectors:**\n- *“Find the latest design document in Google Drive and summarize it.”* [3]\n- *“Check my unread emails from the legal team and draft replies.”* [3]\n\n**Note:** Connectors require authentication and may prompt for approval before sensitive actions (e.g., sending emails) [2].",
