  "answer_markdown": "To hand off your active terminal coding session to a cloud-based repo you haven’t cloned locally, use the **Vibe CLI** to teleport your session to **Vibe Code Web**. Run the following command in your terminal (assuming you have the [Vibe CLI installed](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/install-setup)) to continue your work remotely without local files or setup [1][3][5]:\n\n```bash\nvibe --teleport\n```\n\n### What you give up by using **Vibe Code Web** instead of a local editor (e.g., VS Code):\n- **Local filesystem/shell access**: The remote session runs in a managed cloud sandbox, so you lose direct access to your local working tree, secrets, or unsupported runtimes [4].\n- **Editor context**: No inline file editing, diffs, or source control integration (e.g., Git commits/pushes must be done via the web interface) [4].\n- **Non-interactive scripting**: The CLI supports unattended runs with `vibe --prompt`, but Vibe Code Web does not [4].\n- **Session persistence**: Your terminal session state (e.g., open files, shell history) is not preserved; the cloud session starts fresh against the GitHub repo [3].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Send a prompt to a cloud session from the Vibe CLI, or teleport an active CLI session to the web."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Continue the session I started in the CLI on the web."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "Navigate to your project root and run:\n\n```bash\nvibe\n```"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "Repository access | Local clone | Local clone | Directly via GitHub"
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "After you describe the outcome you want in natural language when using **Vibe Work**, the following happens [1][2][3]:\n\n1. **Vibe gathers context**: It collects relevant information from your prompt, attached files, connected tools, or the web [1].\n\n2. **Vibe plans and acts**: It breaks the task into smaller steps, selects the appropriate tools (e.g., Web Search) without requiring explicit confirmation for non-sensitive actions [1][3], and executes them while showing progress in real time [1].\n\n3. **Approval for sensitive actions**: Before performing sensitive operations, Vibe explicitly asks for your approval [1][2].\n\n### **Control Retained by You**\nYou maintain full control throughout the process [1][2][4]. Specifically:\n- Vibe **shows every tool call** it makes, allowing you to review its actions [1].\n- You can **steer or stop** the process at any point [1].\n- Outputs are **inspectable, editable, and reusable** across sessions [1].\n\nFor example, if you describe a task like *“Find the three most-discussed AI announcements from the past week and summarize them,”* Vibe autonomously picks tools (e.g., Web Search) and executes the steps without further input, but it still seeks approval for sensitive actions [3].",

  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Across every mode, you interact with Vibe **the same way**: same Mistral models, same patterns, same control. A typical Vibe workflow looks like this: 1. **You describe the outcome you want** in natural language. 2. **Vibe gathers context** from your prompt, attached files, connected tools, or the web. 3. **Vibe plans and acts**: it breaks the task into steps, calls the right tools, and shows its progress in real time. 4. **You review and reuse**: outputs are inspectable, editable, and reusable across sessions."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Describe the outcome you want **in natural language**: Work gathers context, breaks the task into steps, calls the right tools, and asks for approval before sensitive actions."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Work breaks the request into steps and starts. It picks the tools it needs (Web Search here) without asking."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

