{
  "answer_markdown": "In the FIM completion operation `POST /v1/fim/completions`, the **required fields** in the `FIMCompletionRequest` request body are:\n\n- `model` (string) — ID of the model with FIM to use [1].\n- `prompt` (string) — The text/code to complete [1].\n\nThe **optional `suffix` field** provides additional context for the model by specifying text/code that comes *after* the `prompt` [1]. When both `prompt` and `suffix` are provided, the model fills in the content **between** them. For example:\n\n```\nprompt = \"def count_words_in_file(file_path: str) -> int:\"\nsuffix = \"return n_words\"\n```\n\nThis would generate the function body between the function definition and the `return` statement [1]. If `suffix` is omitted, the model performs a standard completion starting from the `prompt` [1].",

  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "ID of the model with FIM to use."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "The text/code to complete."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Optional text/code that adds more context for the model."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "When given a `prompt` and a `suffix` the model will fill what is between them."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "When `suffix` is not provided, the model will simply execute completion starting with `prompt`."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

