message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "All models listed in the Mistral model capability matrix support batching, as indicated by the **Batch** column marked 'yes' for each model [1]. This includes:

- Codestral (all versions)
- Devstral (all versions)
- Magistral (all versions)
- Ministral (all versions)
- Mistral (all versions, including embeddings and moderation models)
- OCR models
- Pixtral
- Voxtral
- Z.ai GLM 5.2

For example, the **Mistral Embed** model explicitly lists batching as a supported feature [3], and **Mistral Moderation 2** also confirms batching support [4].

To use batching, you can either:
1. **File Batching** (for up to 1 million requests):
   ```python
   created_job = client.batch.jobs.create(
       input_files=[batch_data.id],
       model="mistral-small-latest",
       endpoint="/v1/chat/completions",
       metadata={"job_type": "testing"}
   )
   ```
   [2]

2. **Inline Batching** (for fewer than 10,000 requests):
   ```python
   inline_batch_data = [
       {
           "custom_id": "0",
           "body": {
               "max_tokens": 128,
               "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is the best French cheese?"}]
           }
       },
       {
           "custom_id": "1",
           "body": {
               "max_tokens": 512,
               "temperature": 0.2,
               "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is the best French wine?"}]
           }
       }
   ]

   created_job = client.batch.jobs.create(
       requests=inline_batch_data,
       model="mistral-small-latest",
       endpoint="/v1/chat/completions",
       metadata={"job_type": "testing"}
   )
   ```
   [2]
",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Codestral Embed (https://docs.mistral.ai/models/codestral-embed-25-05) | yes"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
