  "answer_markdown": "When the included monthly usage on your plan runs out **without** pay-as-you-go enabled, Vibe Code (and API access) can stop functioning until the next billing period or until an admin changes the settings, depending on the plan type. This is because pay-as-you-go is off by default, and some Pro plans purchased through partners (e.g., Google, Apple, Free Mobile, Orange) **cannot enable pay-as-you-go** at all, meaning Vibe Code will stop once the included usage is exhausted [1].\n\nWhen the **Organization monthly spending limit** is reached instead, API access (including Vibe Code) is suspended for the entire Organization until the next month begins or an admin increases the limit. This applies across all Workspaces and is independent of the included monthly usage or pay-as-you-go settings [3][4].\n\n### Key Differences:\n1. **Included monthly usage exhausted (pay-as-you-go off):**\n   - Vibe Code/API access may stop until the next billing period or admin intervention [1][2].\n   - Some plans (e.g., partner Pro plans) **cannot enable pay-as-you-go**, so access stops permanently until the next billing period [1].\n\n2. **Organization spending limit reached:**\n   - API/Vibe access is **suspended for the entire Organization** until the next month or admin action [3][4].\n   - This is a **hard cap** enforced at the Organization level, regardless of individual Workspace limits or pay-as-you-go settings.\n\n### Workspace-Specific Spending Limits:\nIf a **Workspace-specific spending limit** is reached (not the Organization limit), API access for **only that Workspace** is suspended until the next month or admin adjustment [6][7].",
